WEBVTT

00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:09.583
Ah, she's waking up.

00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:12.083
Huh?

00:01:13.208 --> 00:01:15.417
It's so warm and soft...

00:01:15.417 --> 00:01:17.083
No, it's not like that!

00:01:17.083 --> 00:01:19.417
Miss Meme was doing
this until just a moment ago.

00:01:19.417 --> 00:01:21.208
Then she said her legs
were falling asleep,

00:01:21.208 --> 00:01:24.042
so I had no choice but to switch with her!

00:01:24.708 --> 00:01:26.750
Sorry about that.

00:01:28.792 --> 00:01:30.875
Is this the hospital?

00:01:30.875 --> 00:01:34.375
Yes. She's being operated
on right now in there.

00:01:34.375 --> 00:01:36.542
Operated on?

00:01:40.542 --> 00:01:43.125
Miss Eternal Feather...

00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:46.375
Then I didn't dream it.

00:01:48.083 --> 00:01:53.792
Earlier, Sid-<i>sensei </i>questioned us,
about Miss Eternal Feather.

00:01:53.792 --> 00:01:56.917
He asked if she
was troubled by anything,

00:01:56.917 --> 00:02:01.375
or if she had anything to do with
anyone up to no good, and so forth.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:05.458
Miss Tsugumi, can you think
of anything that rings any bells?

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:11.250
No, nothing. Right now,
I can't think of <i>anything</i>.

00:02:12.292 --> 00:02:15.625
What do we do?
If she passes away like this...

00:02:15.625 --> 00:02:18.875
You must not say
anything to jinx her, Tsugumi.

00:02:18.875 --> 00:02:22.333
Sid-<i>sensei </i>said not to worry.

00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:25.417
Apparently, DWMA has
an in-house doctor of darkness,

00:02:25.417 --> 00:02:28.625
and he is a cracker-jack physician.

00:02:28.625 --> 00:02:30.292
You mean it?

00:02:30.292 --> 00:02:35.833
It's that doctor who is doing the surgery.
So I'm sure she'll be okay.

00:02:35.833 --> 00:02:37.333
Oh, yeah?

00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:40.125
It's just that he's
quite an unusual fellow,

00:02:40.125 --> 00:02:42.792
and has even overhauled his own body.

00:02:42.792 --> 00:02:45.750
There are terrifying rumors
that he secretly collects cadavers,

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:49.042
and repeatedly carries out
experiments in creating zombies.

00:02:49.042 --> 00:02:50.208
Zombies?!

00:02:50.208 --> 00:02:51.792
Mwaaah!

00:02:51.792 --> 00:02:55.542
But then, even if she survives,
you can't help but feel sorry for her!

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:57.792
Miss Tsugumi, you must not give up hope!

00:02:57.792 --> 00:03:02.250
Um, what are they again,
with the arms held straight outward? Yeah!

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.750
There's a chance
that she could be someone

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.667
who's just fine,
as long as we hold our breath!

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:07.958
It's the same either way!

00:03:07.958 --> 00:03:12.375
Right now, the only thing
we can do is have faith and wait.

00:03:12.375 --> 00:03:14.333
You're right.

00:03:20.625 --> 00:03:27.250
<i>we wanna be there even if we had to</i>
<i>twist the world all around to get there</i>

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:38.125
<i>without you, i guess i couldn't</i>
<i>even find the future here today</i>

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:49.125
<i>i was always trying to take nothing for granted</i>

00:03:49.125 --> 00:03:57.125
<i>for the day i might lose them</i>

00:03:57.125 --> 00:04:04.167
<i>but you just came in to my black</i>
<i>and white monochrome destiny</i>

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:14.375
<i>and colored it all over</i>

00:04:15.208 --> 00:04:21.708
<i>we won't be satisfied with the routine future</i>

00:04:21.708 --> 00:04:29.167
<i>we were born to make a new history come true</i>

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:36.333
<i>there's absolutely no</i>
<i>absolute thing in this world</i>

00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:40.917
<i>this road goes on forever</i>

00:04:40.917 --> 00:04:47.042
<i>as long as we won't give up</i>

00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:53.417
When it happened,

00:04:53.417 --> 00:04:56.250
how did Eternal Feather
appear to be behaving?

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.667
Behaving, huh?

00:04:57.667 --> 00:05:00.250
It's like she was
there in body, but not in spirit.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:03.708
Mm-hmm. When I called
out to her, she didn't respond.

00:05:03.708 --> 00:05:06.250
It was almost like
she was being controlled.

00:05:07.958 --> 00:05:09.625
Yeah.

00:05:09.625 --> 00:05:12.917
Did you happen to see any
suspicious-looking figures about?

00:05:12.917 --> 00:05:15.792
There were a lot of
people throughout the bazaar, so,

00:05:15.792 --> 00:05:17.208
I'm not sure.

00:05:17.208 --> 00:05:19.667
What about, say, this woman?

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:20.958
Oh!

00:05:20.958 --> 00:05:24.417
You've already got a suspect?
Way to go, Akane!

00:05:24.417 --> 00:05:28.625
Hmm... Seems like
I might have seen her, but still...

00:05:28.625 --> 00:05:33.667
So what's the deal with her?
Is she gonna be EAT's next target?

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:38.458
Her case is in the investigation
stage over at Central Intelligence.

00:05:38.458 --> 00:05:42.125
They haven't released
any information to EAT yet.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.708
Go ahead and leak it!
It'll boost my grade.

00:05:47.708 --> 00:05:49.333
How much are you paying?

00:05:49.333 --> 00:05:50.417
Hey, you guys!

00:05:50.417 --> 00:05:51.625
No cheating!

00:05:51.708 --> 00:05:54.667
"Tsugumi Spiral!"

00:05:58.792 --> 00:06:03.167
According to what we were told,
the operation should be over by now.

00:06:09.708 --> 00:06:12.042
You're all here accompanying her?

00:06:12.042 --> 00:06:13.833
Yes.

00:06:13.833 --> 00:06:15.917
I am finished.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:36.208
Doctor, sir, is she all right?

00:06:36.208 --> 00:06:38.500
A good question...

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.667
Gagantous!

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.958
He's got a screw in his head!

00:06:46.917 --> 00:06:50.417
She is in the next room. Follow me.

00:06:50.417 --> 00:06:53.500
You haven't remade
her into anything weird, right?

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:57.083
She's still under the
anesthesia, so she's asleep.

00:06:58.542 --> 00:07:00.208
Ma'am...?

00:07:00.708 --> 00:07:02.208
Gagantous!

00:07:02.208 --> 00:07:04.208
She has a screw in her head!

00:07:04.208 --> 00:07:08.042
How could you do such a thing?!
That poor girl!

00:07:08.042 --> 00:07:10.958
Plus, she can't roll over while
she's sleeping, now, can she?!

00:07:10.958 --> 00:07:13.417
She would be better off
as a zombie than like this!

00:07:13.417 --> 00:07:16.750
If she can't roll over,
I can make her a special pillow.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:18.583
Was I out of line?

00:07:18.583 --> 00:07:22.417
No, she is a girl, to be sure.
She would have made a cute zombie,

00:07:22.417 --> 00:07:24.583
maybe even a sexy one.

00:07:24.583 --> 00:07:26.833
Sure, she may still be alive...

00:07:26.833 --> 00:07:31.208
But once she comes to,
how do we explain this to her?

00:07:31.208 --> 00:07:33.250
It's fake!

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:35.167
Are you surprised?

00:07:35.167 --> 00:07:37.083
Well, of course we are!

00:07:37.083 --> 00:07:40.208
But at least she's the
same person she's always been.

00:07:40.208 --> 00:07:43.917
Yeah, but almost <i>too</i>
much like she's always been.

00:07:44.917 --> 00:07:49.833
You even fixed her braid?!
Or is that an extension?

00:07:52.458 --> 00:07:55.000
Her braid is moving on its own!

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.583
Pretty cool, huh?

00:07:56.583 --> 00:07:58.875
What is the meaning of this?!

00:07:59.375 --> 00:08:04.083
You two, her braid is
starting to write something!

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:05.458
"Jesús Navas"

00:08:05.458 --> 00:08:07.417
Jesús Navas?!

00:08:07.417 --> 00:08:09.250
What is it? What does it mean?!

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.750
Is it her dying message?!

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:12.667
She's not dead!

00:08:32.208 --> 00:08:34.875
It's like something
out of <i>The Thing</i>!

00:08:34.875 --> 00:08:38.542
Come on, Miss Anya, move faster!

00:08:38.833 --> 00:08:40.500
Wah! Miss Tsugumi,
pick it up, pick it up!

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.625
Gah! I can't!
I can't, I can't, I can't!

00:08:42.625 --> 00:08:43.958
Whoa!

00:08:43.958 --> 00:08:45.583
Hold on, Meme!

00:08:45.583 --> 00:08:48.917
Wah! He's smiling!

00:08:49.167 --> 00:08:53.000
This is cruel! How could you
turn her body into a toy like this?!

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:54.958
You fiend! You devil!
You embankment pumpkin!

00:08:54.958 --> 00:08:57.417
Now, now, I'm just kidding.

00:08:57.417 --> 00:09:00.125
The actual girl is in here.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:01.792
Huh?

00:09:03.833 --> 00:09:06.833
She has a screw in her head!

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:19.208
Now, I did manage to
preserve her life,

00:09:19.208 --> 00:09:22.458
but she will have to remain
in the hospital for a while.

00:09:22.458 --> 00:09:25.542
The wound on her neck was
deeper than any I would have believed

00:09:25.542 --> 00:09:28.042
that she could inflict on herself.

00:09:28.042 --> 00:09:31.375
Why would she do such a thing?

00:09:31.375 --> 00:09:33.708
Because she couldn't sell her clothes?

00:09:33.708 --> 00:09:35.042
No, it couldn't be that.

00:09:35.042 --> 00:09:37.458
I'm sure that's under
investigation right now,

00:09:37.458 --> 00:09:41.458
but it doesn't change the
fact that she also injured others.

00:09:42.292 --> 00:09:44.542
Depending on the reason for that,

00:09:44.542 --> 00:09:48.417
it may be some time
before she returns to DWMA.

00:10:35.583 --> 00:10:37.250
Yes?

00:10:37.625 --> 00:10:39.042
Ah, Sid?

00:10:39.042 --> 00:10:41.875
She's alive, thanks to you, Dr. Stein.

00:10:41.875 --> 00:10:45.292
Don't be silly... or so I'd say,

00:10:45.292 --> 00:10:48.958
but we had an agreement that you'd
only bring me autopsy work, right?

00:10:48.958 --> 00:10:51.625
This girl is in the NOT class.

00:10:51.625 --> 00:10:55.083
You have to feel bad for her,
getting caught up in shady doings.

00:10:55.083 --> 00:10:58.208
You're the only doctor
who could have saved her life.

00:10:58.208 --> 00:11:01.917
Besides, while her friends
may have been afraid of you,

00:11:01.917 --> 00:11:03.792
they were grateful.

00:11:03.792 --> 00:11:07.958
If you were to come to DWMA,
it would help out tremendously.

00:11:07.958 --> 00:11:10.333
Are we back to that again?

00:11:12.417 --> 00:11:17.000
I'm more cut out for research
than I am for being a teacher.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:22.375
So, was there anything suspicious
left behind on the girl's body?

00:11:22.375 --> 00:11:24.583
Yeah, about that...

00:11:24.583 --> 00:11:27.250
I hated to do this
to a girl of her tender age,

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:29.875
but I looked over every inch of her,

00:11:29.875 --> 00:11:32.917
and there was a very tiny wound,
like she was pricked by a needle,

00:11:32.917 --> 00:11:35.333
on the index finger of her left hand.

00:11:35.333 --> 00:11:37.000
Any toxins within her body?

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.875
No, nor was there any
sign of mental unbalance.

00:11:39.875 --> 00:11:44.542
She has no memory of the event, either.
If I had to make a guess,

00:11:44.542 --> 00:11:47.583
I'd chalk it up to an
undetectable amount of toxin,

00:11:47.583 --> 00:11:51.000
combined with some
kind of suggestive mind control.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:52.417
You mean, magic?

00:11:52.417 --> 00:11:55.167
Well, I can't say that much.

00:11:55.167 --> 00:11:58.083
But there's nothing abnormal about her now.

00:11:58.083 --> 00:12:00.833
I believe returning her to her regular life soon

00:12:00.833 --> 00:12:04.333
would be the most
mentally soothing for her.

00:12:17.333 --> 00:12:21.042
Whoo! We are into summer, all right!

00:12:21.042 --> 00:12:25.875
This burning sun sure is
different from the one in Japan, huh?

00:12:29.708 --> 00:12:31.542
Miss Kana, summer-style!

00:12:31.542 --> 00:12:32.708
Perhaps.

00:12:32.708 --> 00:12:34.458
That's so cute.

00:12:34.458 --> 00:12:36.542
Do you like those ears?

00:12:40.375 --> 00:12:42.000
Not really.

00:12:44.667 --> 00:12:47.292
I'll bet she really does like them.

00:12:47.292 --> 00:12:49.250
What's that you're doing?

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:51.458
At your age,
are you still playing in the water?

00:12:51.458 --> 00:12:55.083
Miss Anya...
This is called water sprinkling.

00:12:55.083 --> 00:12:58.375
You scatter water about
the yard to cool things off.

00:12:58.375 --> 00:13:01.583
I don't think that doing
so brings the temperature down.

00:13:01.583 --> 00:13:06.583
No, it's true! It doesn't
make it that dramatically cooler,

00:13:06.583 --> 00:13:09.042
but it's all about the
aesthetic experience, you know?

00:13:09.042 --> 00:13:12.458
Aesthetic experience?
What do you mean by that?

00:13:12.458 --> 00:13:15.833
Let's see... for example...

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:25.625
Get it?

00:13:25.625 --> 00:13:27.667
I don't understand it at all.

00:13:27.667 --> 00:13:29.792
Hmm. Well, for one thing,

00:13:29.792 --> 00:13:32.667
Miss Anya, your outfit
looks too hot to me.

00:13:32.667 --> 00:13:35.000
I'm fine just the way I am!

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:38.250
In that case, watch.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.833
Aesthetic experience...
Aesthetic experience...

00:13:40.833 --> 00:13:42.667
Wah! Stop!

00:13:44.167 --> 00:13:46.375
Eternal Feather, ma'am!

00:13:46.375 --> 00:13:48.417
You got discharged today?

00:13:48.417 --> 00:13:50.292
If you'd said something,
we would have picked you up.

00:13:50.292 --> 00:13:53.208
It's okay, you don't
have to concern yourselves.

00:13:53.208 --> 00:13:55.458
It did leave a little bit of a scar,

00:13:55.458 --> 00:13:58.792
but at DWMA,
scars are badges of honor, right?

00:13:59.792 --> 00:14:03.500
It's nothing at all, okay? See?

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:07.250
She has a screw in her back!

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:09.750
I guess when Dr. Stein said
wearing a wind-up key out of there

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:13.167
would go over well, he was
right, wasn't he?

00:14:13.167 --> 00:14:15.708
Does this face say
"went over well" to you?

00:14:15.708 --> 00:14:17.750
Please, don't ever do that again.

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:21.333
Ah, ma'am! You're out of the hospital!

00:14:21.333 --> 00:14:23.333
I'm so glad you're feeling better!

00:14:23.333 --> 00:14:26.250
Thank you.
You're looking well, too, Miss Meme.

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:29.333
Yes! Oh, but...

00:14:29.792 --> 00:14:33.708
Have to... celebrate...
your discharge... sometime...

00:14:33.708 --> 00:14:35.167
Miss Jacqueline?

00:14:35.167 --> 00:14:37.458
Ma'am, what's the matter?

00:14:37.458 --> 00:14:40.625
You look like
it's the end of the world.

00:14:40.625 --> 00:14:43.167
Kim and I have broken up.

00:14:45.792 --> 00:14:50.292
Huh? Hold on, Kim!
What do you mean, break up?

00:14:50.292 --> 00:14:53.708
Our getting together
happened too fast.

00:14:53.708 --> 00:14:56.792
We still didn't know
each other well enough.

00:14:56.792 --> 00:14:58.208
That's why we teamed up--

00:14:58.208 --> 00:15:00.542
to understand
each other better, didn't we?

00:15:00.542 --> 00:15:03.250
If there's some problem
with me, come out and tell me,

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.542
and I'll try to make it better!

00:15:05.542 --> 00:15:08.167
It's nothing you've done, Jacqueline.

00:15:08.167 --> 00:15:11.167
It's just that I can't put up with this.

00:15:11.167 --> 00:15:14.958
Put up with what?
So it <i>is </i>a problem with me!

00:15:14.958 --> 00:15:16.708
In any event,

00:15:16.708 --> 00:15:21.167
I need some space right now.
Please understand.

00:15:24.333 --> 00:15:28.375
After we became partners,
we were doing so well together.

00:15:28.375 --> 00:15:31.167
What am I going to do?!

00:15:38.208 --> 00:15:41.708
She asked you to give her a
little space, right?

00:15:41.708 --> 00:15:45.083
Maybe some time will
solve all of this, you know?

00:15:45.083 --> 00:15:47.750
And if not time, maybe the climate?

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:51.250
And if not the climate...
the temperature?

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:53.333
Huh? What do you mean?

00:15:53.333 --> 00:15:57.458
Once you've cooled down,
I'm sure Miss Kim will reach out to you.

00:15:57.458 --> 00:15:59.500
Once I've cooled down?

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:04.042
Ah! And I've got just the
thing for cooling things down!

00:16:04.583 --> 00:16:06.083
A wind chime!

00:16:06.083 --> 00:16:07.875
What is that?

00:16:07.875 --> 00:16:08.958
A bell?

00:16:08.958 --> 00:16:10.417
Oh, you know...

00:16:10.417 --> 00:16:13.542
For the moment,
just listen to its tones, please.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:22.917
Doesn't that feel cool, Tsugumi?

00:16:22.917 --> 00:16:25.542
What cooling sounds those are.

00:16:25.542 --> 00:16:26.667
Huh?!

00:16:26.667 --> 00:16:29.042
How do you get cooler by
listening to those bell sounds?!

00:16:29.042 --> 00:16:33.167
Sounds can't make you any cooler,
can they?! They just go "ding-ding."

00:16:34.125 --> 00:16:35.458
There, you see?

00:16:35.458 --> 00:16:38.000
Aesthetic experience,
aesthetic experience...

00:16:39.792 --> 00:16:43.125
Let those two be. Let's go inside
and get something cold to drink.

00:16:43.125 --> 00:16:46.333
Yes. I'm positively parched.

00:16:56.792 --> 00:16:58.417
Wait up, Miss Anya!

00:16:58.417 --> 00:17:00.167
We're coming, too!

00:17:04.083 --> 00:17:07.000
"Key points notebook"

00:17:55.417 --> 00:17:57.458
Tsugumi!

00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.458
Hey!

00:17:59.458 --> 00:18:01.125
Meme?

00:18:01.125 --> 00:18:03.375
Miss Tsugumi!

00:18:04.333 --> 00:18:05.708
Miss Anya?

00:18:05.708 --> 00:18:08.750
Tsugumi, do you have a minute?

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:11.208
Miss Tsugumi! Over here!

00:18:11.208 --> 00:18:12.542
Tsugumi!

00:18:12.542 --> 00:18:14.542
Miss Tsugumi!

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:17.708
Miss Tsugumi, hurry, this way!

00:18:17.708 --> 00:18:22.792
Come on, Tsugumi, over here!
Here, kitty, kitty, kitty!

00:18:22.792 --> 00:18:26.083
Miss Tsugumi!
I have some delicious cake!

00:18:26.083 --> 00:18:30.083
Come on, Tsugumi! Here we go! Fetch!

00:18:30.083 --> 00:18:31.917
--Come on, Tsugumi, go get it!
--Miss Tsugumi! Jingle-jingle!

00:18:31.917 --> 00:18:34.458
Who am I, a Pochi?

00:18:38.125 --> 00:18:39.417
Miss Tsugumi, this is what happens

00:18:39.417 --> 00:18:42.083
when you take forever to choose a partner.

00:18:42.083 --> 00:18:44.583
She's right, Tsugumi.

00:18:44.583 --> 00:18:46.625
You, too, Meme?

00:18:46.625 --> 00:18:50.000
Please don't go thinking that
we will just wait forever.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:51.917
<i>I'll </i>be waiting.

00:18:51.917 --> 00:18:53.583
You big sneak!

00:18:53.583 --> 00:18:56.958
I mean, I'll be waiting, too.

00:18:57.583 --> 00:19:02.875
But ultimately, only one
person can make the decision.

00:19:06.417 --> 00:19:09.667
You both are awfully strong.

00:19:09.667 --> 00:19:12.625
After having done
nothing since I've gotten here,

00:19:12.625 --> 00:19:16.292
I'd be embarrassed
to be either of your partners.

00:19:16.292 --> 00:19:19.792
I'd have to at least be strong
enough to protect you,

00:19:19.792 --> 00:19:21.833
and be able to produce a blade, first...

00:19:21.833 --> 00:19:23.500
Those are excuses.

00:19:24.292 --> 00:19:28.500
Do you think it will be
that easy to grow stronger?

00:19:30.917 --> 00:19:35.458
Tsugumi, could you
transform into a halberd?

00:19:35.458 --> 00:19:38.167
Huh? Okay...

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:06.500
Miss Meme!

00:20:28.375 --> 00:20:31.458
You two are both incredible.

00:20:31.458 --> 00:20:33.792
For as long as I can remember,

00:20:33.792 --> 00:20:36.625
I've been engaged in strict training.

00:20:36.625 --> 00:20:38.375
Miss Meme probably has been, too.

00:20:38.375 --> 00:20:41.042
Though I've forgotten about it.

00:20:41.042 --> 00:20:42.792
Thinking that you're
going to grow strong enough

00:20:42.792 --> 00:20:46.667
to protect us on
your own is presumptuous!

00:20:47.083 --> 00:20:49.875
If you really want to protect someone,

00:20:49.875 --> 00:20:51.417
the quickest way is to choose a partner,

00:20:51.417 --> 00:20:55.792
and grow stronger
together with them, Tsugumi.

00:20:56.042 --> 00:20:58.708
Do you have that resolve?

00:20:58.792 --> 00:21:01.208
It can't be just about enjoying yourself!

00:21:01.208 --> 00:21:03.042
It's because you're running away,

00:21:03.042 --> 00:21:05.125
making excuses about
wishing to be stronger someday...

00:21:05.125 --> 00:21:09.333
It's because you have no resolve,
Miss Tsugumi, that you have no blade!

00:21:18.167 --> 00:21:19.917
I don't...

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:30.583
But still, I mean, right now...

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:36.083
No one is saying to choose right now.

00:21:36.083 --> 00:21:38.542
We're not even saying
until the end of summer.

00:21:38.542 --> 00:21:39.958
Huh?

00:21:39.958 --> 00:21:42.583
Commoners have a harvest
festival on October 31st,

00:21:42.583 --> 00:21:45.792
called "Halloween," right?

00:21:45.792 --> 00:21:50.375
So until that day, when DWMA holds
its culture festival, the Battle Festival,

00:21:50.375 --> 00:21:52.917
it's either Miss Meme, or me.

00:21:52.917 --> 00:21:56.542
Please choose one or the
other for your partner on that day.

00:21:57.667 --> 00:22:00.292
Uh, right.

00:22:00.375 --> 00:22:02.542
Understood.

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:11.000
Weapon and meister are two in one.
You don't have to worry alone.

00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:13.083
I'm sorry.

00:22:14.083 --> 00:22:18.333
Ah! You're getting the
jump on me again, Miss Meme!

00:22:27.500 --> 00:22:29.583
You're hungry, aren't you?

00:22:29.583 --> 00:22:30.625
Mm-hmm.

00:22:30.625 --> 00:22:33.833
Please make supper
for us today, Miss Tsugumi.

00:22:33.833 --> 00:22:35.000
Okay.

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:36.667
I'll give you a hand.

00:22:36.667 --> 00:22:40.667
Eh?! Well, I'll give you a hand, too!

00:22:47.542 --> 00:22:51.708
<i>With a big wave and a "See you,"</i>

00:22:51.708 --> 00:22:58.625
<i>let's meet in the new day</i>

00:23:15.375 --> 00:23:19.542
<i>Our shadows stretch along the pavement</i>

00:23:19.542 --> 00:23:23.542
<i>coming together, then apart, then together</i>

00:23:23.542 --> 00:23:31.875
<i>What do I say when the road home ends?</i>

00:23:31.875 --> 00:23:36.042
<i>You are not alone. Nope, right nearby,</i>

00:23:36.042 --> 00:23:40.167
<i>there are eyes looking back at you</i>

00:23:40.167 --> 00:23:44.292
<i>And just like a miracle,</i>

00:23:44.292 --> 00:23:48.042
<i>they can turn even failures into laughter</i>

00:23:48.042 --> 00:23:52.167
<i>Thank you for a fun day</i>

00:23:52.167 --> 00:23:56.500
<i>Let's do it again tomorrow</i>

00:23:56.500 --> 00:24:00.583
<i>We'll open a brand-new door</i>

00:24:00.583 --> 00:24:04.750
<i>chasing after dreams and love</i>

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:10.375
<i>and those nameless feelings, too</i>

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:20.417
So then, what happens
on the next Soul Eater Not!

00:24:20.417 --> 00:24:21.375
Sweltering Nights!

00:24:21.375 --> 00:24:22.083
Oblivious!

00:24:22.083 --> 00:24:23.417
Three-man Baseball!

00:24:23.417 --> 00:24:26.042
From Death City with Love! Four stories!

00:24:26.042 --> 00:24:29.125
Pumpkins grow
better when you sing to them.

00:24:29.125 --> 00:24:32.192
"Next time: Pumpkin Growing!"
Eh? Gagantous!
